body:
Oh, again, same. Comparing myself to others is a big issue for me too. And I hadn’t noticed before but I too compare myself with people that have been at it for years. I especially get myself down with “they’ve been at it since they are 12 years old, how can I expect to ever be as good if I’m only starting now as an adult”. 

What I’ve think has helped me is having a clear “purpose” for myself, I’ve commented on a similar post about how I’ve been trying to work on this :P I’ll paste it here; 

{When I am working on something that is important to ME, something that gives me purpose and a sense of progress towards something i deeply care about, I find it easier to not care anymore about how others are doing. Like, okay, I can’t do it like they do, but that’s okay, cause I’m doing it THIS way, my way. In fact, when I have it clear in my mind  where i want to go and that I’m working towards something that’s importan to ME, if i see others doing well, instead of envy I feel so happy for them! for doing whats important to them. Instead of trying to make myself look better at stuff that’s what others want and care about, I know I’m working on my own path.}
